// Type-checks the test suite alongside src/.
//
// The build config (tsconfig.json) deliberately includes ONLY src/**/*.ts —
// it drives `outDir: dist`, and test/ must never be emitted. That is correct
// and must stay that way. The consequence, though, was that nothing type-checked
// test/ at all: 188 test files compiled by tsx at runtime with no static gate,
// so stubs silently drifted behind the production interfaces they impersonate.
//
// This config closes that hole: same strict options, noEmit, and a rootDir wide
// enough to hold every file the program reaches. It is check-only and never
// produces output.
//
// rootDir is ".." (the repo root), not "." — test/alertPriorityWebMirror.test.ts
// deliberately imports ../web/src/alertPriority.ts to prove the server and web
// copies of the priority ladder agree, so the program legitimately spans both
// packages. With noEmit, rootDir has no effect on output layout; it only drives
// the containment check, and TS6059 would otherwise reject that cross-package
// import. Narrowing it back to "." would mean deleting a real mirror test.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"]
}
